    "body": "## Summary\n\nFinal commit of ADR-050. Marks the ADR as Implemented with a **layout-tree-verified delta** — a new verification category this session.\n\n## The verified delta\n\n```\n.vector-pinned-container computed style:\n  display = block         <- was none (from top-level rule only)\n```\n\nThat rule exists **only** inside `@supports (display: grid)`. Pre-ADR-050 the block was dropped entirely. Post-ADR-050 the gate fires, the rule enters cascade, and source order makes it win over the earlier `display: none`.\n\n**Stronger than an aggregate rules-count check**: a rule that could never have reached the cascade without ADR-050 is now reaching it.\n\n## Honest limitation\n\n**First-viewport PNG delta**: not yet verified. `.vector-pinned-container` has `display: block` now, but its ancestors still have culling rules:\n\n- `.vector-main-menu-landmark { display: none }` for the first `.vector-pinned-container`\n- `.vector-column-start h=0` for the second (from ADR-028's earlier diagnostic)\n\n**The `@supports` gate is unblocked**, but the TOC visually rendering depends on ancestor-display work (follow-up).\n\n## The verification category ledger\n\nADR-050 introduces a **sixth category**:\n\n| Category | Example | How verified |\n|---|---|---|\n| PNG-verified (first-viewport) | ADR-042, ADR-043 | PNG screenshot |\n| PNG-verified (scroll) | ADR-045 | scroll-PNG |\n| Behaviorally-complete, visually-subtle | ADR-044 | caveat |\n| Behaviorally-complete, visually-zero (consumer pending) | ADR-047, ADR-048 | caveat (consumer absent from HTML) |\n| **Layout-tree verified (consumer present, blocked by ancestor)** | **ADR-050** | **element computed style** |\n| Measured, no target, deferred | ADR-049 | decision record |\n\n## What shipped\n\n### Commit 1 — `@supports` parse + evaluator\n\n- Capability tables for properties + pseudos\n- `unsupported_value()` — rejects `round`/`sqrt`/`sin`/`cos`/`tan`, `dotted`/`dashed`\n- Recursive `feature_query_supported()` — `not`/`or`/`and`/`selector(...)`/`(prop: value)`\n- `parse_supports_block()` — top-level + `@media`-nested\n- **Critical fix**: recursion inside outer-paren-stripped branch — `not ((A) or (B))` correctly returns false when both supported, preventing double-rendered icons from ADR-047 mask + fallback background-image\n\n### Commit 2 — 15 tests\n\n**Load-bearing test**: `not ((mask-image) or (-webkit-mask-image))` returns false → block dropped → no double-rendered icons.\n\n### Commit 3 — Docs\n\n- ADR-050 → Implemented\n- Post-ADR-050 note in ADR-027 (22 of 73 blocks are `@media`-wrapped)\n- README row + CHANGELOG entry\n\n## Test count\n\n- Before ADR-050: 611 cases / 2386 assertions\n- After Commit 1: unchanged (behavior-neutral)\n- After Commit 2: 626 / 2407 (+15 / +21)\n- After Commit 3: unchanged (docs only)\n\n## Deferred\n\n- Runtime feature detection (probe-based)\n- `@supports selector(...)` complex args\n- Nested `@supports` inside `@supports` (0 uses)\n- `@supports font-tech(...)` / `font-format(...)`\n\nRefs #231\n",
